Producer authentication and the independent closure reconstruction are clean: both producer hashes, the immutable image key, all mounted tree hashes, all 14 ordered identities/spans/hashes, and the inventory digest match. My source-level classification is also converging on 13 definitions plus one relevant domain lemma; the “derived lemma” proof was run only after the main proof used the rule, so it cannot qualify as first-proved.
