The locked binaries are present, but the sandbox exposes a split PID namespace: Lean asks `/proc/<namespace-pid>/exe` while the mounted `/proc` indexes host PIDs, so it cannot locate its own executable. I found a contained audit-only workaround: preload a tiny `getpid` shim that returns the host PID from `/proc/self/status`; it changes no candidate or generated source and makes Lean’s executable discovery address the mounted `/proc` correctly. I’ll record and test the shim before rerunning the required gates.
