/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/str.k-42-
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/str.k-43-  // ==== lexicographic order: < / <= / > / >= by code point (= Python str order on the code
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/str.k-44-  // model). strLt reduces on GROUND code-seqs (krun) but is inert/OPAQUE on symbolic ones
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/str.k-45-  // (a proof's codesProj(V) is an abstract IntSeq — no constructor rule matches), so a symbolic
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/str.k-46-  // str `<` stays a trusted opaque term the way sortVS / intFloatDiv do. Additive: fires only on
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/str.k-47-  // str </<=/>/>= comparisons.
